;; cljfmt — the canonical Clojure formatting rule set. Identical in both
;; sibling repos surveyed, adopted verbatim rather than re-derived: formatting
;; is a rule, not a preference, and a config nobody has to argue about is worth
;; more than a bespoke one.
;;
;; Scope, as with clj-kondo, is a positive allowlist passed on the command line
;; (LINT_CLJ_PATHS in lint.mk) — generated and vendored trees are never handed
;; to the formatter, so there is no ignore list here to drift.
{:indentation? true
 :insert-missing-whitespace? true
 :remove-consecutive-blank-lines? true
 :remove-surrounding-whitespace? true
 :remove-trailing-whitespace? true
 :sort-ns-references? true}
